// Round 4 of the 2026-10-12 benchmark hit this asymmetry twice, in two separate runs of
// 18-money-decimal: `val x: decimal = 19.99` is the natural wrong attempt for that task and got a
// bare type mismatch, while `= 1` got the suffix spelled out. One agent reported finding `19.99d`
// only by carrying the suffix over from the int message. Both paths now say it.
fn main() {
    val a: decimal = 19.99
    val b: bigint = 5.0
    print(1)
}
